From: A. Donz <Avrova@Donz.si>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: allow using the packaged nanobind source

Upstream-Status: Downstream (openRuyi packaging; avoids network access during build)
Upstream-Reference: https://github.com/iree-org/iree/blob/v3.8.0/runtime/setup.py

The runtime build obtains nanobind through CMake FetchContent. Let the source
RPM provide the exact pinned nanobind source tree instead.

--- a/runtime/setup.py
+++ b/runtime/setup.py
@@ -325,5 +325,11 @@
             get_env_cmake_list("IREE_EXTERNAL_HAL_DRIVERS", ""),
             get_env_cmake_option("IREE_ENABLE_CPUINFO", "ON"),
         ] + list(extra_cmake_args)
+        nanobind_source_dir = os.getenv("IREE_NANOBIND_SOURCE_DIR")
+        if nanobind_source_dir:
+            cmake_args.append(
+                f"-DFETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_NANOBIND={nanobind_source_dir}"
+            )
+        cmake_args.append("-DBENCHMARK_ENABLE_TESTING=OFF")
         add_env_cmake_setting(cmake_args, "IREE_TRACING_PROVIDER")
         add_env_cmake_setting(cmake_args, "IREE_TRACING_PROVIDER_H")
